# GhostNet Message Flow Rebuild Plan

## Root Cause Analysis

The message sending is broken due to **3 compounding bugs**:

### Bug 1: [app.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/app.js) sendMessage never persists to backend
The [sendMessage](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/ghostnet-chat.js#72-109) function in [app.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/app.js) (line 163-191) sends via GhostChat encryption through WebSocket, but **never calls [persistMessage()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/app.js#117-152)** (the HTTP POST to `/message`). This means:
- Messages are only sent via raw WebSocket routing
- No database persistence happens
- If recipient is offline, message is **lost forever**
- Conversation list never updates

### Bug 2: Server WS handler sends "offline" error instead of storing
The server's WebSocket `'message'` handler (line 585-642) returns an error to the sender when the recipient is not in `connectedPeers`. While it does save to DB afterward, the error message misleads the frontend.

### Bug 3: No pending message delivery on connect
When a user connects and registers via WebSocket, the server never checks for pending messages that were stored while they were offline.

## Fix Plan

### 1. Server ([ghostnet-server.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/ghostnet-server.js))
- Fix `/validate-node` to only reject truly unregistered nodes (not offline ones)
- Fix WS `'message'` handler: always store, don't error on offline
- Add pending message delivery on WebSocket registration
- Fix `/message` endpoint: don't reject messages to offline but registered nodes

### 2. Frontend ([app.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/app.js)) 
- Make [sendMessage](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/ghostnet-chat.js#72-109) always call HTTP persistence (`POST /message`)
- Remove GhostChat encryption layer from send path (simplify)
- Keep WS for real-time delivery only (server handles this after HTTP persist)

### 3. UI ([ui.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/ui.js))
- Fix validation error message: "Node not found" only for unregistered 
- Fix [submitNewChat](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/ui.js#398-480) to allow chat with offline but registered nodes

### 4. Mesh ([ghostnet-mesh.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/ghostnet-mesh.js))
- No changes needed (transport layer is fine)
